 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? It depends on the country. In the Netherlands, much of the language is similar. In Norway, very little. The Dutch spoken in Netherlands is very different from the Dutch spoken in Suriname or the Caribbean, and Norwegian is completely different from Danish. It' a bit like comparing Spanish and Portuguese. That's usually the biggest challenge. Dutch has a lot of soft glottals, while Norwegian is full of hard consonants. Dutch TV is full of series with big subtitles. Norwegian has few popular novels, but they' often in English. If you like the sound of it, go for it. Just learn some basic grammar and you can get by.",
